P-14: root's kind is `fake-acp`, whose definition names an ACP program
(`acp: python3 .arbos/agents-defs/fake_acp.py`). The kernel is the ACP
client: the user's inbox file wakes root, the program thinks, reads
hello.txt through fs/read_text_file, reports a tool call, asks permission
to write (mode auto allows), writes out.txt through fs/write_text_file,
streams a reply, ends the turn. Expect: thinking, tool, assistant, and
turn_complete lines on root's transcript; out.txt written.
State travels as dot-arbos/ (the repo ignores .arbos/); the runner renames
it. hello.txt sits beside it and is copied into the place by the runner
(any file at the fixture's top level other than the fixture's own).
